WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.249
The so-called Twitter files, which

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.449
were written by a group of

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:04.829
independent journalists, given

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:06.419
access to internal company

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.399
documents, offer a behind the scenes

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.809
glimpse at how the federal

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.129
government shaped the flow of

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.929
information on one of the world's

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.119
largest social media platforms.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.739
Whether or not the Twitter files

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.119
contain information that was

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.459
surprising to those already aware

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.809
of the thousands of takedown

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.609
requests the company receives every

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.259
month from law enforcement agencies

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.059
and the courts, or of the immense

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.009
challenges of content moderation

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:30.869
is beside the point.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.669
Twitter files have brought important

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.169
new information to light.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.209
They show that the company stifled

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.399
debate over important policy issues

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.169
by shadow banning certain accounts

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.999
for no good reason and then

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.069
misleading the public about it.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.839
They show that Twitter was routinely

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.729
strongarmed by the White House and

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.769
the FBI into complying

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:51.629
with frivolous takedown requests,

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.489
and they provide evidence

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.929
that the intelligence community

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.849
likely influenced the decision

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.649
to suppress the Hunter Biden laptop

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:00.809
story in the lead up to the 2020

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.009
election.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.030
I mean, to be totally frank,

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.199
almost every conspiracy theory that

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.549
people had about Twitter turned out

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:09.550
to be true.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.620
So

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:15.779
is there a conspiracy theory about

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.039
Twitter that didn't turn out to be

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:17.819
true?

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.589
Conspiracy theorists are often

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:21.599
sloppy with the facts and exaggerate

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.769
what really happened.

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.299
But the information brought to light

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.889
by the Twitter files should be

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.509
alarming to anyone who cares about

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:28.510
free speech and a free society.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:31.049
Government meddling in similar ways

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:33.059
on YouTube, Facebook, Instagram,

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:34.109
and Google Search.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.669
How can we prevent the Internet from

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:38.399
turning into a centralized apparatus

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.499
through which state actors can shape

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.889
and censor public debate?

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:44.779
Here are three major takeaways

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.249
from the Twitter files.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.229
One: twitter distorted

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.999
the conversation and misled the

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.889
public. Twitter had a system of

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:53.779
white lists and blacklists

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.399
that allowed its algorithms and

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.409
human moderators to turn

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.479
engagement dials up and down

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:01.129
based on their users.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:02.689
It used this power to limit the

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:03.889
ability of certain groups and

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.599
individuals to reach an audience,

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.699
including conservative commentator

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:10.069
Dan Bongino, Stanford economist

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:11.290
and medical school professor Jay

00:02:11.291 --> 00:02:12.291
Battacharya,

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.289
MNRA vaccine critic Alex Berenson

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:16.290
and the Libs of TikTok.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.879
When asked if Twitter Shadow bans,

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.309
then co-founder and CEO Jack Dorsey

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:23.779
misled Congress.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.065
Social media is being rigged to

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:27.829
censor conservatives.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:29.419
Is that true of Twitter?

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:30.259
No.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:32.269
Twitter Shadow Banning Prominent

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:33.270
Republicans.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:35.339
Bad.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.299
Is that true?

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:36.972
No.

00:02:36.973 --> 00:02:37.981
The company sought to cover by
tapdancing around

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:40.739
the meaning of the word.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.629
In a 2018 blog post, Twitter's

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.549
trust and Safety team wrote

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:46.199
"We do not shadow ban.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.579
We were always able to see the

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.319
tweets with no follow.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.369
Although you may have to do more

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.199
work to find them, like go

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.179
directly to their profile."

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.159
Needless to say, making tweets

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.539
so hard to find.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.069
Digging through someone's profile is

00:02:59.070 --> 00:02:59.983
the only way to unearth them is

00:02:59.984 --> 00:03:01.949
what's commonly known as shadow

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.049
banning, or as Twitter employees

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.959
termed it, with an Orwellian flair,

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.879
"visibility filtering." The Twitter

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.439
files show the company's staff

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.209
became increasingly comfortable

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.159
using these tools to manage

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.599
the flow of information and

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.759
political discourse around the 2020

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.619
election. Regularly deploying

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:21.269
filters to limit the visibility of

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.979
Trump's tweets and many others

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.449
pertaining to election results in

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:26.339
the weeks preceding the January 6

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.379
riot and the decision to evict

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:30.119
the president from the platform.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.189
Yes, Twitter is a private company

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.659
and it has every right to label the

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.849
tweets of Harvard epidemiologist

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:37.799
Martin Kulldorf as misleading

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.899
when he tweets. Statements such as

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.069
"Thinking that everyone must be

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.839
vaccinated is a scientifically

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.519
flawed, is thinking that nobody

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.709
should." But Twitter is still worthy

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:48.749
of our condemnation,

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:49.750
Dr. Battacharya was shadow banned
despite

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.679
being a respected epidemiologist

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.389
from a prestigious university, and

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:55.859
many of his warnings during the

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:58.019
pandemic turned out to be correct.

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.939
And you can acknowledge serious

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.859
problems with the work of former

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.239
New York Times reporter Alex

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.399
Berenson, who, for instance, badly

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.349
misinterpreted data to infer a spike

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.389
in vaccine caused mortality

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:10.949
while still believing it's

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.019
preferable to have a public airing

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:14.729
of controversial and deeply flawed

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:15.659
arguments.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.369
A better way to deal with speech you

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:19.199
disagree with is to respond

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.299
to it, as Derek Thompson attempted

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.219
to do in the Atlantic when he

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.019
called Berenson "The Pandemic's

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:27.089
Wrongness Man." Ironically,

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:28.949
Twitter raised Berenson profile

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.809
by allowing him to inhabit the role

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:32.389
of the oppressed truth seeker.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.759
Two: The government is secretly

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.169
policing speech.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.459
The most troubling thing about the

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.109
Berenson De-platforming isn't

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:42.119
Twitter's decision per say,

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.859
but whether it made that decision

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:45.719
freely. Was it done at the behest

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:46.799
of the federal government?

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.149
The Twitter files provide

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.529
circumstantial evidence that the

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:51.089
White House played a role when the

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.679
Biden administration took over.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.749
One of their first meeting requests

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:56.369
with Twitter executives was on

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.409
COVID, writes journalist David Zweig

00:04:58.410 --> 00:04:59.459
in the Twitter files.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:01.529
The focus was on anti-vaxxer

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.479
accounts, especially Alex

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:04.528
Berenson.

00:05:04.529 --> 00:05:06.009
"The only pandemic we have is among

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:07.010
the unvaccinated

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.449
and that Americans are killing

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:10.049
people.".

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:11.902
Berenson was suspened hours

00:05:11.903 --> 00:05:12.903
after Biden made those comments.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.539
The leak also revealed that a series

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.309
of meetings took place last December

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:19.619
in which an angry Biden team

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.479
excoriated Twitter executives

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.339
because they were not satisfied

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.929
with its enforcement approach and

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.729
wanted Twitter to do more and to

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:28.979
deplatform several accounts.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:30.809
In Twitter file six, Matt

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:32.939
Taibbi described Twitter as an FBI

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:34.439
subsidiary.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:36.539
Agents from a dedicated task force

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.399
would regularly send lists of

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.319
accounts, some with fewer than 1,000

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:42.299
followers, for Twitter to look at

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.579
for terms of service violations,

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:46.239
such as this left leaning account

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.119
jokingly telling Republicans to

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.829
vote a day late.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:51.839
Former Twitter trust and safety head

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.849
Yoel Roth was in weekly

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.499
meetings with the FBI, Department of

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.389
Homeland Security, and the Office

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.439
of the Director of National

00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.399
Intelligence.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.169
In return for the company's work

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.348
handling FBI requests, Twitter

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:05.519
received $3.4 million

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.589
between October 2019 and early

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:08.999
2021.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.889
Yes, complying with something in

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:12.779
the range of 8,000 requests would

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.639
have required significant resources

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:15.419
from Twitter.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:16.769
And there's no reason the government

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:18.329
shouldn't have to pick up the tab.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:20.159
But should this arrangement

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.869
really exist at all in a free

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:24.089
society given the mission creep

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:25.949
the Twitter files exposed?

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.749
Internal communications in the lead

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:29.549
up to Twitter's decision to stop a

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:31.079
blockbuster New York Post story

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:32.579
about the contents of Hunter Biden's

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.649
laptop from being shared

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:35.729
was also alarming.

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:37.589
Jim Baker, the former FBI

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:39.329
lawyer then working at Twitter,

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.129
leaned on Yoel Roth to treat the

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.989
laptop as the likely result

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:44.609
of a Russian hack and leak

00:06:44.610 --> 00:06:46.859
operation. Despite little evidence

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:48.779
that claim the FBI

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:50.699
had told Roth to expect just such

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:52.289
a foreign operation to drop in

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:54.059
October and that Hunter Biden would

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:55.229
be a likely target.

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:56.909
A month before the laptop story

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:58.799
broke, Roth even participated

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.689
in a tabletop simulation at the

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:02.549
Aspen Institute about how

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:04.859
to handle a Hunter Biden data dump.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.749
Publicly, 51 former

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:08.459
intelligence officials, including

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:10.649
James Clapper, Michael Hayden

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.509
and John Brennan, published a letter

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:14.369
claiming that the laptop has

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:16.169
all the classic earmarks of a

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:18.449
Russian information operation.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:19.919
The New York Post story turned out

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:21.479
to be completely true.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.189
With all that pressure coming from

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:24.599
supposedly reputable and

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.399
knowledgeable sources was Twitter

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.259
really acting independently when it

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:29.639
suppressed the story?

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:30.899
Giving the government unfettered

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.759
access to exert pressure behind the

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.769
scenes turned a forum for free

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:35.999
discussion with all of the

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.259
unavoidable messiness and

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:38.969
misinformation that free speech

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:41.429
entails into something much worse,

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:42.929
a state approved narrative

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:43.889
Generator.

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:45.779
Three: Twitter permitted

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:47.489
covert state propaganda on its

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:48.509
platform.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:50.249
The U.S. ran sock puppet accounts on

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:51.449
Twitter and then may have tried to

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.039
shut them down secretly when it

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.149
looked like it was caught in the

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:56.489
act. After Trump won the 2016

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:58.379
election and Clinton blamed Russia

00:07:58.380 --> 00:07:59.399
for her loss.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.439
Congress began to focus intently

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:02.669
on the role of foreign

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:04.409
misinformation on the Internet.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:06.359
Twitter began transparently labeling

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:07.739
accounts associated with any

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:08.889
government. Whether it be a

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:10.599
politician or a state run media

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:12.399
outlet. It also pledged to Congress

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:14.349
to rapidly identify and shut down

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:15.969
all state backed covert information

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:18.399
operations and deceptive propaganda.

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:19.629
But apparently that didn't always

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:21.669
extend to propaganda disseminated by

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:22.809
our own government.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:24.879
As the Intercept's Lee Fang revealed

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:27.189
the US Central Command, CENTCOM

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:29.229
asked Twitter to white list a number

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:31.149
of Arab language accounts spreading

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.189
messages in support of the US

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.109
backed Yemen war so that

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:36.399
they would get the same special

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:37.959
treatment that verified accounts

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:39.729
received. Twitter complied.

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:41.589
One whitelisted account described

00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:42.459
accurate U.S.

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:44.019
drone strikes that only hit

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:45.039
terrorists.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.509
At first, the accounts had an

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:48.039
attached disclosure, noting that

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:49.419
they were linked to the US

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.039
government. But that disclosure was

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:52.269
eventually dropped from many

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:53.769
accounts and at least one

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:55.449
whitelisted government sock puppet

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.519
account used an AI generated image

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:58.899
as a profile picture.

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:01.059
An internal email thread shows

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:02.229
that the Department of Defense

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:03.999
wanted to meet with Twitter's legal

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.799
team in a secure facility.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:07.149
One member of Twitter's team

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:09.009
speculated that the agency wanted

00:09:09.010 --> 00:09:10.779
to classify its work with Twitter to

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:12.159
avoid embarrassment.

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:13.989
Baker suspected that the fake

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:15.609
accounts were set up using poor

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:17.289
tradecraft and that they wanted to

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:19.359
wind down the operation without

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:20.529
revealing accounts.

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.599
Connection to the DOD.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:24.579
So what should Americans demand

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.529
of Congress in light of the Twitter

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:27.819
file revelations?

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:29.829
Lawmakers should rein in the FBI

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:31.719
and other executive agencies with

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:34.119
stricter reporting requirements

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:36.159
and defund any federal task force

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:37.959
whose mission includes fighting the

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:40.989
slippery concept of misinformation.

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:42.519
And yet, that will probably never

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:44.709
happen. The new omnibus bill just

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:46.549
increased the FBI funding.

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:48.099
Unfortunately, if a tool of

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:49.929
centralized speech control can be

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:51.729
abused by government, it's a virtual

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:53.649
certainty that it will be

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:54.939
abused eventually.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.199
We should follow the advice of

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.239
Julian Assange and the Cypherpunk

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.979
movement that shaped his thinking,

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.869
which maintained that technology,

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:04.179
not government policy, is the only

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:06.129
effective check on authoritarian

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:07.413
tendencies in the long run.

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:10.509
You can't trust the government to

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:12.169
implement the policies that it says

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.029
it is implementing.

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:15.369
And so we must provide

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:18.159
the underlying tools, cryptographic

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:20.559
tools that we control

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:22.719
as a sort of use of force.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:23.652
Good news is that many people are

00:10:23.653 --> 00:10:25.539
gradually waking up to the

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:27.039
dangers of allowing a company to

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:28.989
maintain centralized control over

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:30.339
the public conversation.

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:32.079
After Trump's deplatforming, many

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:33.669
conservatives migrated to the

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:35.709
encrypted network Telegram

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:37.449
since Elon Musk's takeover of

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:38.949
Twitter. Many progressives have

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.357
joined the decentralized platform

00:10:40.358 --> 00:10:41.358
Mastodon.

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:43.599
Former Twitter CEO Jack Dorsey

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.669
has invested in the blockchain based

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:47.619
social media site Noster and

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:49.539
published an article calling for a

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.549
native Internet protocol for social

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.349
media, arguing that social media

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:55.059
must be resilient to corporate and

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:57.189
government control and moderation

00:10:57.190 --> 00:10:59.409
is best implemented by algorithmic

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:00.189
choice.

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:01.839
And if Elon Musk wants to keep

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.759
Twitter relevant and competitive in

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:05.169
this continually fracturing

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:07.329
landscape and live up to his promise

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:09.009
of bringing more free speech to the

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:10.389
platform, he will have to take these

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:12.069
developments seriously and think

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:14.229
about ways that Twitter 2.0

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:15.459
can avoid the fate of its

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:17.529
predecessor by once again falling

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:20.289
victim to state interference.

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:22.209
He should aim to design a platform

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:23.529
that makes this kind of meddling

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:25.419
impossible so that we don't have

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:27.219
to trust any tech executive,

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:29.229
including Elon Musk, not

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:30.819
to censor speech on behalf of the

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:31.820
government.

